    "available_at": "2026-10-15T14:38:30.207870+00:00",
    "body": "More companies are increasing their use of used pallets , according to Modern Materials Handling’s annual pallet survey , with 35% of respondents saying they use more than a year ago. In the previous survey, 18% reported an increase.\nThe findings come from the 2026 Pallet Market Evaluation, produced by Peerless Research Group . The survey included 115 MMH readers who work at locations that use pallets.\nMany respondents already use wood pallets in their day-to-day operations. Nearly three-quarters (73%) use used or core wood pallets, while 52% purchase new wood pallets, with some companies using both.\nMost respondents have kept their use of used pallets steady: 59% reported no change from a year earlier. Just 6% are using fewer, down from 22% in the previous survey.\nRELATED: Read Modern Materials Handling’s 2026 Pallet Market Evaluation\nQuality and availability remain concerns\nAmong companies buying used pallets, 37% say quality is not as good as with new pallets. Another 22% report fewer available pallets or shortages, while 13% say used wood pallets have become more expensive.\nStill, these experiences aren't universal. One-third of used-pallet buyers say they haven't encountered those problems and don't expect future purchasing difficulties.\nGetting pallets returned is another concern raised in the report. “Usually, I don’t get the pallets back,” one survey participant said, pointing to a recurring need to replace pallets that leave an operation and never return.\nWood remains the top choice\nWood pallets remain in use at 92% of surveyed companies, unchanged from 2025. The standard 48-by-40-inch pallet is the most common size, used by 73% of respondents.\nPlastic pallets gained ground, with 36% of respondents using them, up from 28% last year. Companies can use several materials, so those figures include operations using both wood and plastic.\nPallet pooling also grew to 19% of respondents, up from 16% in the previous survey. Vendors also provide other services: 38% of respondents use on-site recycling and reclamation management, up from 32% last year.",
    "body_sha256": "5f19b6503f3654cd43cf249b669f07d8df27b7856f99a0f4db80cdc76a8c598b",
